# tracker Issue Tracking

This project uses [tracker (tracker-cli)](https://github.com/gastownhall/tracker) for issue tracking.

## Core Rules

- Track ALL work in tracker-cli (never use markdown TODOs or comment-based task lists)
- Use `tracker-cli ready` to find available work
- Use `tracker-cli create` to track new issues/tasks/bugs
- Treat commit, push, and tracker remote sync as policy-controlled handoff actions
- Run `tracker-cli prime` for complete workflow context (SSOT for operational commands)
- Default to conservative git authority: report status and proposed commands unless the user, orchestrator, or repository profile explicitly authorizes commit/sync/push

## Quick Reference

```bash
tracker-cli prime                              # Load complete workflow context (SSOT)
tracker-cli ready                              # Show issues ready to work (no blockers)
tracker-cli list --status=open                 # List all open issues
tracker-cli create "title" -t task -p 2        # Create new issue
tracker-cli update <id> --claim                # Claim work atomically
tracker-cli unclaim <id>                       # Release stuck issue (agent crashed)
tracker-cli close <id>                         # Mark complete
tracker-cli dep add <issue> <depends-on>       # Add dependency
tracker-cli tracker push                          # Sync with remote when authorized
```

## Workflow

1. Check for ready work: `tracker-cli ready`
2. Claim an issue atomically: `tracker-cli update <id> --claim`
3. Do the work
4. Mark complete: `tracker-cli close <id>`
5. Handoff: report changed files, validation, issue status, and any proposed commit/sync/push commands

## Issue Types

- `bug` - Something broken
- `feature` - New functionality
- `task` - Work item (tests, docs, refactoring)
- `epic` - Large feature with subtasks
- `chore` - Maintenance (dependencies, tooling)

## Priorities

- `0` - Critical (security, data loss, broken builds)
- `1` - High (major features, important bugs)
- `2` - Medium (default, nice-to-have)
- `3` - Low (polish, optimization)
- `4` - Backlog (future ideas)

## Context Loading

Run `tracker-cli prime` to get complete workflow documentation in AI-optimized format.
`tracker-cli prime` is the single source of truth for operational commands and session workflow.

For detailed docs: see AGENTS.md, the tracker quickstart
(https://github.com/gastownhall/tracker/blob/main/docs/getting-started/quickstart.md), or run `tracker-cli --help`

